# Plans / docs / rules alignment

## Canonical product docs

| Doc | Path |
|-----|------|
| Overview | `docs/product/overview.md` |
| Roadmap | `docs/product/roadmap.md` |
| History (not updated) | `docs/product/history/v1.md`, `v2.md`, `v3.md` |
| Agent product rule | `.cursor/rules/wedge-product.mdc` |

## Skill map

| Need | Skill |
|------|--------|
| Product phases / roadmap | `roadmap-update` |
| Implementation plan (bite-sized + tests) | `writing-plans` |
| Sync docs after landed changes | `docs-updater` |
| Full align after confirmation | `wedge-keep-aligned` |

## When the user confirms a product or scope change

1. Update the matching `docs/product/` file(s).
2. Update `.cursor/rules/wedge-product.mdc` if behavior, language or scope changed.
3. Do not leave rules contradicting docs.

## Do not

- Add cloud/sync, Dock-mode or any new feature to docs without explicit user confirmation and a design doc (see "Focused by default" in `docs/product/overview.md`).
- Invent truncation or higher character limits until discussed (the 40-character cap stays, no truncation).
